# PART 00 — MISSION

WORLD SIGNAL is evolving from a daily global news briefing into a longitudinal intelligence publication.

The existing frontend already supports reading daily editions, inspecting evidence, analyzing relationships, and viewing edition-level changes.

The next step is to make the information genuinely discoverable, traceable over time, and personally useful.

This phase focuses on five major capabilities:

1. Global Intelligence Search.
2. Longitudinal Storyline Tracker.
3. Personal Intelligence Desk.
4. Since Your Last Visit.
5. Arbitrary Edition Comparison.

Also assess the architecture required for a future Evidence Export feature.

This is a functionality and product-experience phase.

Do not spend this phase primarily on another visual redesign.

The priority is meaningful functionality, reliable data handling, intuitive interactions, and polished integration with the existing editorial design system.

A feature is not complete simply because a button exists.

Every interactive element must perform its advertised action.

