## 7.3 Comparison interface

Show:

### Overview

- Previous edition.
- Current edition.
- New signals.
- Materially updated signals.
- Unchanged signals.
- Omitted signals.

### Detailed comparison

Allow filtering by:

- New.
- Updated.
- Unchanged.
- Omitted.

### Signal-level detail

Display:

- Headline changes.
- Claim changes.
- Source changes.
- Confidence changes.
- Importance changes.
- Status changes.
- Relationship changes.
- Narrative changes.

Use the existing reason codes.

### Navigation

Allow opening:

- Previous version of a signal.
- Current version of a signal.

Preserve exact edition and signal IDs in URL state.

## 7.4 Critical omission rule

An omitted signal is not necessarily resolved, closed, or retracted.

Keep the warning visible.

A missing signal in the selected later edition must remain an omission classification unless explicit editorial lifecycle metadata establishes otherwise.

